# global-config-merge-behavior: exercise per-key merge rule end-to-end.
#
# Fixture design (v4.2 rework): assertions live OUTSIDE the replay. Each scenario triggers a real
# bash call that invokes mergeSwarmConfig directly and captures the actual resolved config. The
# lane asserts on the real JSON output, not on pre-scripted narration.
#
# Scenarios A-D (v4.2):
#   A: global has 3-slot pool + rotation; project has 1-slot pool. → project array replaces global.
#   B: same global; project has inheritGlobal: false + full pool. → global fully skipped.
#   C: global is corrupt; project has valid pool. → global_swarm_yml_unreadable + project still applied.
#   D: fresh machine (no global, no project); first root session. → dual scaffold fires.

